  "summary": "Charlottesville City Council heard a six-month update from Police Chief Mike Kochis on the city's Flock ALPR program and informally signaled support for continuing it. Kochis touted a restrictive policy with seven-day retention and monthly audits, and cited uses including stolen vehicle recoveries and shooting investigations.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Charlottesville has one of the most, if not the most, restrictive Flock camera policies in the Commonwealth",
      "paragraph_idx": 5
    },
    {
      "quote": "Data is stored for seven days, and the system is audited monthly by both CPD and the executive director of the Police Civilian Oversight Board.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "Though there was no formal vote, City Manager Sam Sanders gauged the Councilors' stance on continuing the cameras' use.",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
